IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part15-notes.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 4 (annual accounts), Information to be given in notes to the accounts, ss 409 to 413
-- (lines 5282-5384 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- s 409(1) to (3) and s 412(1) to (3) are regulation-making powers (what regulations may require): inert, reason 2. s 410 is blank in this text.

§§ `Information to be given in notes to the accounts`

-- ---- s 409: information about related undertakings -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5293 | (a) that in the opinion of the directors of the company the disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of—
-- src:5294 | (i) that undertaking,
-- src:5295 | (ii) the company,
-- src:5296 | (iii) any of the company's subsidiary undertakings, or
-- src:5297 | (iv) any other undertaking which is included in the consolidation;
-- src:5298 | (b) that the Secretary of State agrees that the information need not be disclosed.
@ref s 409(4) The conditions for not disclosing information about an undertaking outside the United Kingdom (src:5293-5298)
GIVEN `in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of that undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of any of the company's subsidiary undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of any other undertaking included in the consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State agrees that the information need not be disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(4) the conditions for non-disclosure are met` MEANS
    IF (`in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of that undertaking` OR `in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of the company` OR `in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of any of the company's subsidiary undertakings` OR `in the opinion of the directors disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of any other undertaking included in the consolidation`) AND `the Secretary of State agrees that the information need not be disclosed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are— (a) that in the opinion of the directors of the company the disclosure would be seriously prejudicial to the business of"

-- src:5299 | (5) Where advantage is taken of any such exemption, that fact must be stated in a note to the company's annual accounts.
@ref s 409(5) Where advantage is taken of the exemption, the note must say so (src:5299)
GIVEN `advantage is taken of the exemption from disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 409(5) the fact that advantage is taken of the exemption must be stated in a note to the annual accounts` MEANS
    IF `advantage is taken of the exemption from disclosure`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where advantage is taken of any such exemption, that fact must be stated in a note to the company's annual accounts"

-- ---- s 410A: information about off-balance sheet arrangements ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5303 | (1) If in any financial year—
-- src:5304 | (a) a company is or has been party to arrangements that are not reflected in its balance sheet, and
-- src:5305 | (b) at the balance sheet date the risks or benefits arising from those arrangements are material,
-- src:5306 | the information required by this section must be given in the notes to the company’s annual accounts.
@ref s 410A(1) When the information is required (src:5303-5306)
GIVEN `in the financial year the company is or has been party to arrangements that are not reflected in its balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the balance sheet date the risks or benefits arising from those arrangements are material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 410A(1) the information required by section 410A must be given in the notes to the annual accounts` MEANS
    IF `in the financial year the company is or has been party to arrangements that are not reflected in its balance sheet` AND `at the balance sheet date the risks or benefits arising from those arrangements are material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If in any financial year— (a) a company is or has been party to arrangements that are not reflected in its balance sheet, and (b) at the balance sheet date the risks or benefits arising from those arrangements are material, the information required by this section must be given in the notes"

-- src:5311 | (4) If the company is subject to the small companies regime in relation to the financial year (see section 381), it need not comply with subsection (2)(b).
@ref s 410A(4) The small companies regime: the company need not comply with subsection (2)(b) (src:5311)
GIVEN `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime in relation to the financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 410A(4) the company need not comply with subsection (2)(b)` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company is subject to the small companies regime in relation to the financial year (see section 381), it need not comply with subsection (2)(b)" (not subject: the text gives no relief)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the section 381 answer is not known
    `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime in relation to the financial year`

DECLARE `s 410A(2) item of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 410A(2)(a) the nature and business purpose of the arrangements`
    `s 410A(2)(b) the financial impact of the arrangements on the company`

-- src:5307 | (2) The information required is—
-- src:5308 | (a) the nature and business purpose of the arrangements, and
-- src:5309 | (b) the financial impact of the arrangements on the company.
-- src:5310 | (3) The information need only be given to the extent necessary for enabling the financial position of the company to be assessed.
@ref s 410A(2) The information required; (3) only to the extent necessary (src:5307-5310)
GIVEN item IS A `s 410A(2) item of information`
      `s 410A(1) the information required by section 410A must be given in the notes to the annual accounts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the item is necessary for enabling the financial position of the company to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 410A(4) the company need not comply with subsection (2)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 410A(2) the item of information must be given in the notes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 410A(1) the information required by section 410A must be given in the notes to the annual accounts`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (1) applies is not known
    WHEN JUST required THEN
        IF NOT required
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the information required by this section must be given in the notes" applies only if subsection (1) is met
        ELSE IF NOT `the item is necessary for enabling the financial position of the company to be assessed`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information need only be given to the extent necessary for enabling the financial position of the company to be assessed"
             ELSE CONSIDER item
                  WHEN `s 410A(2)(a) the nature and business purpose of the arrangements` THEN JUST TRUE
                  WHEN `s 410A(2)(b) the financial impact of the arrangements on the company` THEN
                      CONSIDER `s 410A(4) the company need not comply with subsection (2)(b)`
                      WHEN JUST relief THEN
                          IF relief
                          THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it need not comply with subsection (2)(b)"
                          ELSE JUST TRUE
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

DECLARE `s 410A(5) the entity whose arrangements are tested` IS ONE OF
    `s 410A(5) the company`
    `s 410A(5) the undertakings included in the consolidation, as if they were a single company`

-- src:5312 | (5) This section applies in relation to group accounts as if the undertakings included in the consolidation were a single company.
@ref s 410A(5) Group accounts: the undertakings included in the consolidation are treated as a single company (src:5312)
GIVEN `the accounts are group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 410A(5) the entity whose arrangements are tested`
`s 410A(5) the entity whose arrangements are tested in the accounts` MEANS
    IF `the accounts are group accounts`
    THEN `s 410A(5) the undertakings included in the consolidation, as if they were a single company`
    ELSE `s 410A(5) the company`

-- ---- s 411: information about employee numbers and costs -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5314 | (1) The notes to a company’s annual accounts must disclose the average number of persons employed by the company in the financial year.
@ref s 411(1) The notes must disclose the average number of persons employed (src:5314)
GIVEN `these are the notes to a company's annual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 411(1) the notes must disclose the average number of persons employed by the company in the financial year` MEANS
    IF `these are the notes to a company's annual accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notes to a company's annual accounts must disclose"

-- src:5315 | (1A) In the case of a company not subject to the small companies regime, the notes to the company’s accounts must also disclose the average number of persons within each category of persons so employed.
@ref s 411(1A) A company not subject to the small companies regime must also disclose the average number in each category (src:5315)
GIVEN `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 411(1A) the notes must also disclose the average number of persons within each category` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime`
    WHEN JUST regime THEN
        IF regime
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company not subject to the small companies regime"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:5316 | (2) The categories by reference to which the number required to be disclosed by subsection (1A) is to be determined must be such as the directors may select having regard to the manner in which the company's activities are organised.
@ref s 411(2) The directors select the categories (src:5316)
GIVEN `the categories are selected having regard to the manner in which the company's activities are organised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 411(2) the categories are ones the directors may select` MEANS
    IF `the categories are selected having regard to the manner in which the company's activities are organised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such as the directors may select having regard to the manner in which the company's activities are organised"

-- src:5317 | (3) The average number required by subsection (1) or (1A) is determined by dividing the relevant annual number by the number of months in the financial year.
@ref s 411(3) The average number (src:5317)
GIVEN `the relevant annual number` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 411(3) the average number` MEANS
    IF `the number of months in the financial year` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the relevant annual number` DIVIDED BY `the number of months in the financial year`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a financial year with no months has no average

-- src:5319 | (a) for the purposes of subsection (1), the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in that month (whether throughout the month or not);
@ref s 411(4)(a) The relevant annual number for subsection (1) (src:5319)
GIVEN `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 411(4)(a) the relevant annual number for subsection (1)` MEANS
    sum `the number of persons employed under contracts of service by the company in each month of the financial year`

-- src:5320 | (b) for the purposes of subsection (1A), the number of persons in the category in question of persons so employed;
@ref s 411(4)(b) The relevant annual number for subsection (1A) (src:5320)
GIVEN `the number of persons in the category in question of persons so employed in each month of the financial year` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 411(4)(b) the relevant annual number for subsection (1A)` MEANS
    sum `the number of persons in the category in question of persons so employed in each month of the financial year`

-- src:5322 | (5) Except in the case of a company subject to the small companies regime, the notes to the company’s annual accounts or the profit and loss account must disclose, with reference to all persons employed by the company during the financial year, the total staff costs of the company relating to the financial year broken down between—
@ref s 411(5) Staff costs: not for a company subject to the small companies regime (src:5322)
GIVEN `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 411(5) the notes or the profit and loss account must disclose the total staff costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 381 the company is subject to the small companies regime`
    WHEN JUST regime THEN
        IF regime
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in the case of a company subject to the small companies regime"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)

-- src:5322 | (5) Except in the case of a company subject to the small companies regime, the notes to the company’s annual accounts or the profit and loss account must disclose, with reference to all persons employed by the company during the financial year, the total staff costs of the company relating to the financial year broken down between—
-- src:5323 | (a) wages and salaries paid or payable in respect of that year to those persons,
-- src:5324 | (b) social security costs incurred by the company on their behalf, and
-- src:5325 | (c) other pension costs so incurred.
@ref s 411(5) The total staff costs broken down between wages and salaries, social security costs and other pension costs (src:5322-5325)
GIVEN `wages and salaries paid or payable in respect of the year to those persons` IS A NUMBER
      `social security costs incurred by the company on their behalf` IS A NUMBER
      `other pension costs so incurred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 411(5) the total staff costs` MEANS
    `wages and salaries paid or payable in respect of the year to those persons` PLUS `social security costs incurred by the company on their behalf` PLUS `other pension costs so incurred`

-- src:5327 | “pension costs” includes any costs incurred by the company in respect of—
-- src:5328 | (a) any pension scheme established for the purpose of providing pensions for persons currently or formerly employed by the company,
-- src:5329 | (b) any sums set aside for the future payment of pensions directly by the company to current or former employees, and
-- src:5330 | (c) any pensions paid directly to such persons without having first been set aside;
@ref s 411(6) "pension costs" (src:5327-5330)
GIVEN `costs in respect of a pension scheme established for the purpose of providing pensions for persons currently or formerly employed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `costs in respect of sums set aside for the future payment of pensions directly by the company to current or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `costs in respect of pensions paid directly to such persons without having first been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 411(6) the cost is a pension cost` MEANS
    IF `costs in respect of a pension scheme established for the purpose of providing pensions for persons currently or formerly employed by the company` OR `costs in respect of sums set aside for the future payment of pensions directly by the company to current or former employees` OR `costs in respect of pensions paid directly to such persons without having first been set aside`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“pension costs” includes any costs incurred by the company in respect of"

-- src:5331 | “social security costs” means any contributions by the company to any state social security or pension scheme, fund or arrangement.
@ref s 411(6) "social security costs" (src:5331)
GIVEN `it is a contribution by the company to a state social security or pension scheme, fund or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 411(6) the cost is a social security cost` MEANS
    IF `it is a contribution by the company to a state social security or pension scheme, fund or arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“social security costs” means any contributions by the company to any state social security or pension scheme, fund or arrangement"

DECLARE `s 411(7) the entity whose employees are counted` IS ONE OF
    `s 411(7) the company`
    `s 411(7) the undertakings included in the consolidation, as if they were a single company`

-- src:5332 | (7) This section applies in relation to group accounts as if the undertakings included in the consolidation were a single company.
@ref s 411(7) Group accounts: the undertakings included in the consolidation are treated as a single company (src:5332)
GIVEN `the accounts are group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 411(7) the entity whose employees are counted`
`s 411(7) the entity whose employees and staff costs are counted in the accounts` MEANS
    IF `the accounts are group accounts`
    THEN `s 411(7) the undertakings included in the consolidation, as if they were a single company`
    ELSE `s 411(7) the company`

-- ---- s 412: information about directors' benefits: remuneration -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5342 | (4) For the purposes of this section, and regulations made under it, amounts paid to or receivable by—
-- src:5343 | (a) a person connected with a director, or
-- src:5344 | (b) a body corporate controlled by a director,
-- src:5345 | are treated as paid to or receivable by the director.
-- src:5346 | The expressions “connected with” and “controlled by” in this subsection have the same meaning as in Part 10 (company directors).
@ref s 412(4) Amounts paid to a connected person or a controlled body corporate are treated as paid to the director (src:5342-5346)
-- "connected with" and "controlled by" have the same meaning as in Part 10 (coa4): borrowed answers.
GIVEN `s 252 the amount is paid to or receivable by a person connected with the director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 255 the amount is paid to or receivable by a body corporate controlled by the director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 412(4) the amount is treated as paid to or receivable by the director` MEANS
    IF `s 362 helper either answer` `s 252 the amount is paid to or receivable by a person connected with the director` `s 255 the amount is paid to or receivable by a body corporate controlled by the director` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "amounts paid to or receivable by— (a) a person connected with a director, or (b) a body corporate controlled by a director, are treated as paid to or receivable by the director"

-- src:5347 | (5) It is the duty of—
-- src:5348 | (a) any director of a company, and
-- src:5349 | (b) any person who is or has at any time in the preceding five years been a director of the company,
-- src:5350 | to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as may be necessary for the purposes of regulations under this section.
@ref s 412(5) The duty of a director, or a former director of the last five years, to give notice to the company (src:5347-5350)
-- "any person who is or has at any time in the preceding five years been a director": the five years run back from the day the duty is asked of.
GIVEN `s 250 the person is a director of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the last day on which the person was a director of the company` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 412(5) the person is under the duty to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 250 the person is a director of the company`
    WHEN JUST director THEN
        IF director
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE formerDirector
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF formerDirector EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a director (section 250) is not known
    WHERE
        formerDirector MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day on which the person was a director of the company`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any director of a company, and any person who is or has at any time in the preceding five years been a director" (never a director)
            WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
                IF lastDay AT LEAST `add years` `the day on which the question is asked` (-5)
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time in the preceding five years been a director of the company"

-- src:5351 | (6) A person who makes default in complying with subsection (5) commits an offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 412(6) Offence: default in complying with subsection (5) (src:5351)
GIVEN `s 412(5) the person is under the duty to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person makes default in complying with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 412(6) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who makes default in complying with subsection (5) commits an offence"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the duty answer is not known and no limb decides
    `s 362 helper both answers` `s 412(5) the person is under the duty to give notice to the company of such matters relating to himself as regulations require` (JUST `the person makes default in complying with subsection (5)`)

-- src:5351 | (6) A person who makes default in complying with subsection (5) commits an offence and is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 412(6) Penalty: summary conviction, a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale (src:5351)
GIVEN conviction IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 412(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER conviction
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale"
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF conviction, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- s 413: information about directors' benefits: advances, credit and guarantees ----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5353 | (1) In the case of a company that does not prepare group accounts, details of—
-- src:5354 | (a) advances and credits granted by the company to its directors, and
-- src:5355 | (b) guarantees of any kind entered into by the company on behalf of its directors,
-- src:5356 | must be shown in the notes to its individual accounts.
@ref s 413(1) A company that does not prepare group accounts: notes to its individual accounts (src:5353-5356)
GIVEN `the company does not prepare group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 413(1) the details must be shown in the notes to the company's individual accounts` MEANS
    IF `the company does not prepare group accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company that does not prepare group accounts"

-- src:5357 | (2) In the case of a parent company that prepares group accounts, details of—
-- src:5358 | (a) advances and credits granted to the directors of the parent company, by that company or by any of its subsidiary undertakings, and
-- src:5359 | (b) guarantees of any kind entered into on behalf of the directors of the parent company, by that company or by any of its subsidiary undertakings,
-- src:5360 | must be shown in the notes to the group accounts.
@ref s 413(2) A parent company that prepares group accounts: notes to the group accounts (src:5357-5360)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company prepares group accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 413(2) the details must be shown in the notes to the group accounts` MEANS
    IF `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the company prepares group accounts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a parent company that prepares group accounts"

-- src:5361 | (3) The details required of an advance or credit are—
-- src:5362 | (a) its amount,
-- src:5363 | (b) an indication of the interest rate,
-- src:5364 | (c) its main conditions, ...
-- src:5365 | (d) any amounts repaid.
-- src:5366 | (e) any amounts written off, and
-- src:5367 | (f) any amounts waived.
@ref s 413(3) The details required of an advance or credit (src:5361-5367)
GIVEN `its amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an indication of the interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its main conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any amounts repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any amounts written off` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any amounts waived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 413(3) the details of an advance or credit are given as subsection (3) requires` MEANS
    IF `its amount` AND `an indication of the interest rate` AND `its main conditions` AND `any amounts repaid` AND `any amounts written off` AND `any amounts waived`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The details required of an advance or credit are— (a) its amount"

-- src:5368 | (4) The details required of a guarantee are—
-- src:5369 | (a) its main terms,
-- src:5370 | (b) the amount of the maximum liability that may be incurred by the company (or its subsidiary), and
-- src:5371 | (c) any amount paid and any liability incurred by the company (or its subsidiary) for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee (including any loss incurred by reason of enforcement of the guarantee).
@ref s 413(4) The details required of a guarantee (src:5368-5371)
GIVEN `its main terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the maximum liability that may be incurred by the company (or its subsidiary)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any amount paid and any liability incurred by the company (or its subsidiary) for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee (including any loss incurred by reason of enforcement of the guarantee)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 413(4) the details of a guarantee are given as subsection (4) requires` MEANS
    IF `its main terms` AND `the amount of the maximum liability that may be incurred by the company (or its subsidiary)` AND `any amount paid and any liability incurred by the company (or its subsidiary) for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee (including any loss incurred by reason of enforcement of the guarantee)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The details required of a guarantee are— (a) its main terms"

DECLARE `s 413 advance or credit` HAS
    `s 413 the amount of the advance or credit` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413 the amount repaid` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413 the amount written off` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413 the amount waived` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `s 413 guarantee` HAS
    `s 413 the maximum liability that may be incurred` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413 the amount paid and the liability incurred for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `s 413(5) totals` HAS
    `s 413(5) the total of the amounts of the advances and credits, subsection (3)(a)` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413(5) the total of the amounts repaid, subsection (3)(d)` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413(5) the total of the amounts written off, subsection (3)(e)` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413(5) the total of the amounts waived, subsection (3)(f)` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413(5) the total of the maximum liabilities of the guarantees, subsection (4)(b)` IS A NUMBER
    `s 413(5) the total of the amounts paid and liabilities incurred, subsection (4)(c)` IS A NUMBER

-- src:5372 | (5) There must also be stated in the notes to the accounts the totals—
-- src:5373 | (a) of amounts stated under subsection (3)(a),
-- src:5374 | (b) of amounts stated under subsection (3)(d),
-- src:5375 | (ba) of amounts stated under subsection 3(e),
-- src:5376 | (bb) of amounts stated under subsection 3(f),
-- src:5377 | (c) of amounts stated under subsection (4)(b), and
-- src:5378 | (d) of amounts stated under subsection (4)(c).
@ref s 413(5) The totals to be stated in the notes (src:5372-5378)
GIVEN advances IS A LIST OF `s 413 advance or credit`
      guarantees IS A LIST OF `s 413 guarantee`
GIVETH A `s 413(5) totals`
`s 413(5) the totals to be stated` MEANS
    `s 413(5) totals` OF sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 413 the amount of the advance or credit`) advances),
                         sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 413 the amount repaid`) advances),
                         sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 413 the amount written off`) advances),
                         sum (map (GIVEN a YIELD a's `s 413 the amount waived`) advances),
                         sum (map (GIVEN g YIELD g's `s 413 the maximum liability that may be incurred`) guarantees),
                         sum (map (GIVEN g YIELD g's `s 413 the amount paid and the liability incurred for the purpose of fulfilling the guarantee`) guarantees)

DECLARE `s 413(5) which total` IS ONE OF
    `s 413(5)(a) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (3)(a)`
    `s 413(5)(b) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (3)(d)`
    `s 413(5)(ba) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (3)(e)`
    `s 413(5)(bb) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (3)(f)`
    `s 413(5)(c) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (4)(b)`
    `s 413(5)(d) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (4)(c)`

-- src:5384 | (8) Banking companies and the holding companies of credit institutions need only state the details required by subsection (5)(a) and (c).
@ref s 413(8) Banking companies and holding companies of credit institutions need only state two totals (src:5384)
GIVEN total IS A `s 413(5) which total`
      `s 1164(2) the company is a banking company, or the holding company of a credit institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 413(8) the total must be stated` MEANS
    IF `s 1164(2) the company is a banking company, or the holding company of a credit institution`
    THEN CONSIDER total
         WHEN `s 413(5)(a) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (3)(a)` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 413(5)(c) the total of the amounts stated under subsection (4)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Banking companies and the holding companies of credit institutions need only state the details required by subsection (5)(a) and (c)"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5379 | (6) References in this section to the directors of a company are to the persons who were directors at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate.
@ref s 413(6) The directors of a company (src:5379)
GIVEN `the person was a director at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 413(6) the person is one of the directors for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the person was a director at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this section to the directors of a company are to the persons who were directors at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate"

-- src:5380 | (7) The requirements of this section apply in relation to every advance, credit or guarantee subsisting at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate—
-- src:5381 | (a) whenever it was entered into,
-- src:5382 | (b) whether or not the person concerned was a director of the company in question at the time it was entered into, and
-- src:5383 | (c) in the case of an advance, credit or guarantee involving a subsidiary undertaking of that company, whether or not that undertaking was such a subsidiary undertaking at the time it was entered into.
@ref s 413(7) Every advance, credit or guarantee subsisting at any time in the financial year (src:5380-5383)
GIVEN `it subsists at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 413(7) the requirements of the section apply to the advance, credit or guarantee` MEANS
    IF `it subsists at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whenever it was entered into, whether or not the person was a director then, and whether or not a subsidiary undertaking was then a subsidiary
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every advance, credit or guarantee subsisting at any time in the financial year to which the accounts relate"
